.TH TDEFLATPAK 1 "November 2026" "tdeflatpak 0.1.0" "Trinity Desktop Environment"
.SH NAME
tdeflatpak \- Flatpak manager for the Trinity Desktop Environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tdeflatpak
.RB [ \-\-updates | \-\-search | \-\-remotes ]
.RI [ "generic TDE and TQt options" ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tdeflatpak
(\(lqFlatpak Manager\(rq) is a graphical application for the Trinity Desktop
Environment (TDE) that manages Flatpak applications, runtimes and remotes.
It uses the libflatpak library directly and works on both the system-wide
installation
.RI ( /var/lib/flatpak )
and the per-user installation
.RI ( ~/.local/share/flatpak ).
.PP
The main window has four tabs:
.TP
.B Installed
Lists installed applications (and optionally runtimes).
Applications can be started and items can be uninstalled.
.TP
.B Search & Install
Searches the AppStream catalogs of all enabled remotes by name, ID or
summary, and installs the selected applications together with the runtimes
they need.
.TP
.B Updates
Checks for updates and installs all or only the selected ones.
.TP
.B Remotes
Lists remotes. Remotes can be added (from a
.I .flatpakrepo
file or URL, or Flathub with one click), enabled, disabled and removed.
Unused runtimes can be removed.
.PP
Changes to the system-wide installation require authorization through
polkit, so a polkit authentication agent such as
.B polkit\-agent\-tde
must be running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-updates
Start with the Updates tab.
.TP
.B \-\-search
Start with the Search & Install tab.
.TP
.B \-\-remotes
Start with the Remotes tab.
.TP
.I file
A
.I .flatpakref
file (install the application it describes) or a
.I .flatpakrepo
file (add the remote it describes). Local paths and URLs are accepted.
.PP
The generic TDE and TQt options are also supported; run
.B tdeflatpak \-\-help\-all
for the complete list.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B tdeflatpak \-\-updates
Open the Flatpak Manager and check for updates.
.TP
.B tdeflatpak https://dl.flathub.org/repo/flathub.flatpakrepo
Add the Flathub remote.
.TP
.B tdeflatpak org.example.App.flatpakref
Install an application from a downloaded
.I .flatpakref
file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/flatpak
System-wide Flatpak installation.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/flatpak
Per-user Flatpak installation.
.TP
.I ~/.trinity/share/config/tdeflatpakrc
Window settings.
